  "content": {
    "id": "p2-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Suppose that $\\triangle ABC$ has vertices at coordinates $A(1,1)$, $B(3,4)$ and $C(4,k)$. Find the values of $k$ if $\\triangle ABC$ is isosceles. Note that there are three cases to consider: $AB=BC$, $AC=CB$ and $BA=AC$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$k=4\\pm2\\sqrt3$, $\\frac76$, $-1$ or $3$.\n\nEquate squared side lengths for each of the three possible equal-side pairs.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}AB^2&=(3-1)^2+(4-1)^2\\\\AB^2&=13\\\\BC^2&=1+(k-4)^2\\\\AC^2&=9+(k-1)^2\\end{align*}$$\nFor $AB=BC$:\n$$\\begin{align*}13&=1+(k-4)^2\\\\(k-4)^2&=12\\\\k&=4\\pm2\\sqrt3\\end{align*}$$\nFor $AC=CB$:\n$$\\begin{align*}9+(k-1)^2&=1+(k-4)^2\\\\k^2-2k+10&=k^2-8k+17\\\\6k&=7\\\\k&=\\frac76\\end{align*}$$\nFor $BA=AC$:\n$$\\begin{align*}13&=9+(k-1)^2\\\\(k-1)^2&=4\\\\k&=-1\\text{ or }3\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 140
  },
